WEBVTT

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.550
Where's Haruka-neesama?

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:04.100
She went out to meet Maki-chan.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.910
Then, what are you doing, Kana?

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:08.810
I'm feeling a bit hungry, so...

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:14.560
Even if you search through such a place, I doubt you'd find any food.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:20.580
Food which is forgotten by everybody, and surprises those who find it, tends to be hidden in these places.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.480
Found it.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:24.880
What's that?

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:28.230
What, I wonder.  It seems I've seen this box before.

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:29.940
Oh?

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:30.710
Or not.

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:32.110
Which one is it?

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.090
That's not important.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:39.180
This ought to be... No, this must be something good!

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:42.620
It won't open.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:43.390
Just give up.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:45.810
I won't give up!

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.380
You insatiable person.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:50.340
"You insatiable person."

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:51.940
How childish.

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:55.280
It's this insatiable desire that will give me the strength to create miracles.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:58.740
Well...

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:01.800
But this thing is really shut tight.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:03.810
Help me out.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.420
What happened to your miracle?

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:07.690
Lend me your power of desire.

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:10.290
I don't have time to play along with your idiocy.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.410
Go find someone else.

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:16.040
Oh? So Chiaki doesn't care about the contents of this treasure?

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:16.960
None whatsoever.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:21.160
All right. Then it won't matter if I claim it for myself, right?

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:22.790
Treasure, huh?

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:26.930
Perhaps there are photos of Chiaki bathing when she was little.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:30.380
This guy's pretty tough...

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:32.590
Hey, hold it in place.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:34.190
I'm holding it.

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:37.980
Ouch...

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:42.710
It hurts.

00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:44.840
I bumped my head hard.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.980
And I bumped my butt, you idiot.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:51.120
More importantly, what's inside the box?

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:56.420
What? What's in there?

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.060
What's inside was...

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:01.090
What was that sound?

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.110
What's wrong?

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.000
I think... I just... stepped on something.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.230
What's that?

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.270
What's this?

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:15.550
Don't you recognize it at all?

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:19.900
Well, this glass rabbit...

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.100
No, I can't remember.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:23.890
It's not yours, Kana?

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:25.090
Nope.

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:28.120
Well, it for sure isn't mine.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:28.910
Which means...

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:33.810
What's wrong?

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:37.570
Did your illness come back due to the curse of the treasure box?

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:40.680
T–This... belongs to Haruka.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.220
Really?

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.760
It wasn't a gift or something like that?

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:47.170
I'm sure of it.

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:50.300
Also, it's something that she has treasured since childhood.

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:52.760
The ear came off.

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:55.640
No! This must be a mistake!

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:58.770
That's right! It's a dream! I must be daydreaming!

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:02.020
Please let me wake up from this dream!

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.440
What are you doing, bastard?!

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.840
This isn't the time to be dreaming.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.110
What are we going to do?

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:11.360
It hurts...

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:12.100
What to do?

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:16.200
Besides, if you hadn't opened it by force, this wouldn't have happened in the first place.

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:19.730
At any rate, you're my accomplice.

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:21.380
Why's that? You're the one who started...

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:22.060
How troublesome.
Why's that? You're the one who started...

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:23.390
How troublesome.

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:25.920
If this continues, it won't be as simple as us getting scolded.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:27.670
That's because you...

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:30.660
Ah, Haruka will be very sad.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:33.240
It'll be worse than her getting mad.

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:35.380
Correct?

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.400
I understand. I'll help too.

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:44.570
Okay!

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.540
Let's get started.

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:50.560
Hey, you... do you really plan to do this?

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.490
It's just reattaching the ear, right?

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:56.290
Please be quiet for a second.

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:02.030
I can do this. I can do this if I put my mind to it.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:03.590
*Gulp*

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:12.300
Hey.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.290
I broke the other ear off too.

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:19.800
You've been way too hard on your big sister!

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:22.850
Shut up! It was a mistake to leave it to you.

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:24.550
Here, let me fix it!

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:25.520
No! I won't let you!

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:28.670
Why are you getting competitive over such things?

00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:30.830
Oh, the tail came off.

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:32.680
W–What the heck are you doing?!

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:35.040
It's because you refuse to let go!

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:38.160
I've never heard of people sneezing at such an important time!

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:41.120
Ah, it's stuck to my hand!

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:43.580
Hey, don't pull so hard!

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:45.970
But I can't get it off!

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:48.110
Then I'll just have to cut off your hands.

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:49.170
Oh, the head came off.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:56.220
Hello, Fujioka? Can you help me look for something? It's very urgent!

00:06:56.920 --> 00:07:00.760
Listen, Keiko. Don't mess it up. It's got to be a cute rabbit!

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:02.260
That's right, Yoshida!

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:05.980
Eh? Uchida? Whatever. Just get me the thing that loves carrots!

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.980
Makoto! The one with carrots!

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:11.490
Run, Touma!

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:21.410
Sorry for having you accompany me on a Sunday.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:25.780
It's nothing. I don't really have anything to do at home, anyway.

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:27.540
That aside, have you made up your mind?

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:30.080
They were all pretty decent.

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:35.190
I know. If you hesitate at times like this, it'll be difficult to come to a decision.

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:36.050
Indeed.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:40.050
Well, hopefully we'll find something nice by the end of the day.

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:45.470
Rabbit, rabbit, rabbit...

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:46.580
Fujioka-kun!

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.320
Ah, hello.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.680
Are you looking for something?

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:52.830
Yeah, I'm looking for a rabbit.

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:53.700
Rabbit?

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.570
Um, I'm in a hurry. See you.

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:58.270
Rabbit...

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:04.930
Isn't this just a general store? He shouldn't have mistaken this for a pet shop.

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:06.800
Oh, yeah! I just remembered something regarding rabbits.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:10.310
I've got to go. Can you wait for me at home?

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:12.800
I've got just the thing!

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:15.960
I got it. Then I'll call you later, okay?

00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:19.900
I see.

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:23.360
So Minami Haruka likes rabbits, huh.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:28.480
But, it's going to take me some time to catch a rabbit.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.070
I'll have to skip school for a bit.

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:37.530
This must be a trial you've set for me, Minami Haruka.

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:39.040
What's that?

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:40.940
Did you see that?

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:43.540
You there, can you come over here?

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:46.820
What's going on?

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:49.250
Don't look over there, Haruka.

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:54.760
They're late.

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:57.520
Why isn't anyone calling?

00:08:57.520 --> 00:08:59.470
Where on Earth did they go to search?

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:07.770
Did Haruka-neesama say when she'll be back?

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:11.470
They're really making me wait.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:15.040
No, it's still early.

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:18.140
Do we really have to wait this long?

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:19.900
Are you okay?

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:21.480
I'm NOT okay!

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:26.500
Hello?

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:28.940
Are you done yet?!

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:30.710
I'm still searching.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:34.030
Quick... hurry... u*agi... bring me!

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.820
What did you just say?

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:37.880
Sorry, the reception isn't that good here.

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:39.850
Bring me u*agi!

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:42.700
Eel? So eel will do?

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:44.690
Just hurry and bring it!

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:46.150
O–Okay, I got it.

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:51.850
Where can I find an eel?

00:09:55.120 --> 00:10:01.990
Kana? Sorry, the rabbit was here just a while ago, but it seems he has gone off somewhere.

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:04.010
I want it!

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:06.720
Then look for it! I must have it no matter what!

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:08.460
Understood, I'll look for him.

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:19.920
I've found it, Kana-chan! I'll be getting it right away!

00:10:20.410 --> 00:10:22.530
Good. It seems you're the fastest, Uchida!

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:24.220
Keep up the good work!

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:25.420
Yup, I'll do my best!

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:30.510
Kana, I got it! I got it, Kana!

00:10:31.070 --> 00:10:33.060
Keep it up!

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.360
Eh? I'm running already.

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:43.770
Good! Don't waste any time!

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:45.530
Leave it to me!

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:50.300
Why do I have to run in the first place?

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:54.350
We'll be getting a new one in no time.

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:56.210
Will things really work out?

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:58.960
Just leave it to me!

00:11:01.880 --> 00:11:03.110
I'm home!

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:05.540
What?! She's back already?

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:07.530
Welcome back!

00:11:07.530 --> 00:11:09.430
That was fast.

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:10.730
Welcome back.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:14.770
Yeah, there's something I want to give to Maki so I'm back to get it.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:17.630
Oh? What might that be?

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:20.320
A rabbit necklace made out of glass.

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:22.850
Have you seen it?

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:34.040
This is bad. What do we do?

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:36.020
We'll just have to wait for Uchida and the others.

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:36.780
You're right.

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:37.250
Yes.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:41.290
Before they get here, all we can do is...

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:43.330
Buy them some time.

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:44.330
Yeah.

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:46.190
What's wrong?

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:47.970
U–Uh, no, it's nothing.

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:53.050
Haruka-neesama, is that glass necklace shaped like a rabbit?

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:55.810
That's right. Have you seen it?

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:03.260
Hmm, I wonder where I put it.

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:05.970
I kind of remember putting it away in the kitchen...

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:09.820
Now, now, that's enough of the chit-chat.

00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:14.510
Since you just came back, let's have some tea first.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:17.500
S–Sure.

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:22.840
I'll go make the tea.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:24.770
You're right, thank you.

00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:26.970
You're welcome.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:29.770
So, what did you go to buy?

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:33.920
Actually, Maki's relative's birthday is coming up,

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:35.660
so we went to buy a present.

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:37.470
Ah, I see!

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:43.280
Yeah, but Maki is having a hard time finding the right gift.

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:46.590
That's why I thought about giving her something I have from home.

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:50.030
Are you all right, Chiaki?

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:53.220
I'm fine.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:13:00.430
Geez, Chiaki. You're so clumsy.

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:05.240
They're here!

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:07.720
Eh? They're here? Who?

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:11.060
Kana-chan, I've got it!

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:13.670
You got it?

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:17.730
It was worth waiting for you, Uchida. Good, good, good, good!

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.000
It cost me 2,000 yen, too.

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:23.380
Great job! I'll pay you back ten-thousand fold one day!

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:26.210
It's really cute.

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:28.620
Little animal that loves carrots.

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:34.010
Oh my, that's so cute.

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:35.640
Welcome, Uchida-san.

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:37.140
Hello.

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:39.790
Come back after you've found the right one, moron!

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:43.630
Why?

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:46.270
Is that all she came here for?

00:13:46.270 --> 00:13:48.490
Uchida is really busy today, apparently.

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:49.490
I see.

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:53.760
Yeah, it's got to be in the kitchen. I remember I left it there.

00:13:57.420 --> 00:14:00.780
Chiaki, what are you doing sitting there?

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:03.600
Oh, so it has finally started.

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:05.130
What has?

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:08.420
Training. This is training.

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:12.530
Training? Um... Kana?

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:16.650
Her tests are coming, so she said she wants to improve her concentration.

00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:21.280
They said on TV that the best place to improve concentration is the kitchen, remember?

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:23.850
Is that so?

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:27.530
Oh, that might be Maki.

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:28.810
I'll pick it up!

00:14:28.810 --> 00:14:31.820
Oh, okay. Then please do.

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:33.800
Haruka-neesama.

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:35.870
What is it?

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:39.810
Perhaps you left it in your own room and forgot about it.

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:42.850
But...

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:45.250
You're right. I'll go have a look.

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:53.690
There's something I'd like to ask.

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:57.210
If it's for eating, do natural ones taste better?

00:14:57.670 --> 00:14:58.640
Huh?

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:01.560
Natural ones seem harder to get.

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:04.920
But I have gotten some great tips.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:08.660
I heard I'll be able to catch a lot if I went to this fishing spot, so I'm here to check it out.

00:15:09.490 --> 00:15:11.660
I'll do my best to catch a big one.

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:14.180
Eh? Minami?

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:22.680
Yes, this is Minami.

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:25.600
Well, I did find it.

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:25.610
Really?
Well, I did find it.

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:27.050
Really?

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:33.210
Yeah... but he says he's still working, so he can't leave yet.

00:15:33.210 --> 00:15:33.900
Usa?

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:36.920
What should I do?

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:38.940
This is amazing, Kana.

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:40.580
I keep winning!

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:43.060
What in blue blazes are you doing?

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:45.750
But I just keep on winning!

00:15:47.430 --> 00:15:49.660
What should I do with these?

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:59.620
Hey, I've been running the whole time, when can I stop?

00:15:59.990 --> 00:16:01.610
Keep running until you find it!

00:16:01.610 --> 00:16:02.600
Find it?

00:16:04.550 --> 00:16:05.300
Find what?

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:11.180
I'm sorry about just now.

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:14.050
This time I'll get one even cuter.

00:16:14.050 --> 00:16:15.110
Okay, Kana-chan?

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:19.650
Eh, Kana-chan? Hello? Hello?!

00:16:23.390 --> 00:16:25.060
I can't find it there either.

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:28.620
That call wasn't from Maki?

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:31.750
It was from Uchida calling to say thanks.

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:34.230
She said, "Sorry to have disturbed you."

00:16:34.230 --> 00:16:36.510
What a well-mannered child she is.

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:40.350
Yeah, surprising, isn't it? She actually has that side to her.

00:16:41.740 --> 00:16:44.560
But I'm glad it wasn't Maki who called.

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:48.080
I can't tell her that I forgot where I put it.

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:49.980
Yeah, that's true.

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:54.850
If it's not in my room, then it should be in the kitchen.

00:16:54.850 --> 00:16:57.910
Sorry, coming through.

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:05.880
Since it has come to this, I'll have to do it myself!

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:13.150
Where did I put it?

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:14.450
Haruka-neesama.

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:15.540
What is it?

00:17:15.540 --> 00:17:18.090
Don't you want to take a break?

00:17:18.090 --> 00:17:21.540
Well, I'd like to, but...

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:22.260
Chiaki.

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:24.870
I'm going.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:26.160
Understood.

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:27.650
Are you going out?

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:29.110
For a bit.

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:30.990
Don't be too late.

00:17:32.520 --> 00:17:34.940
Train on my behalf, too.

00:17:36.390 --> 00:17:37.200
Understood.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:43.410
Focus the mind. Focus the mind.

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:55.330
Oh, good afternoon.

00:17:55.330 --> 00:18:00.040
It's you, Fuyuki. Oh, right, do you have a rabbit necklace?

00:18:00.570 --> 00:18:02.220
One made of glass.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:05.000
A rabbit necklace?

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:07.100
Such a thing, I...

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:09.350
I guess not.

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:10.650
Well, see ya.

00:18:11.810 --> 00:18:13.200
Goodbye...

00:18:36.430 --> 00:18:37.480
Chiaki.

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:39.420
Yes, Haruka-neesama?

00:18:39.420 --> 00:18:45.820
Sorry to interrupt your training, but can you let me check the drawer behind you?

00:18:45.820 --> 00:18:47.830
Yes, Haruka-neesama.

00:18:49.800 --> 00:18:53.480
I'll go get it. Carry on with your training for a little while, Chiaki.

00:18:57.720 --> 00:18:59.350
Yes, this is Minami.

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:01.940
Oh, Keiko-san!

00:19:02.380 --> 00:19:04.350
Eh? Why are you apologizing?

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:09.120
Rabbit?

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:13.940
Um... hold on a sec.

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:33.910
Chiaki. Which rabbit... is she referring to?

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:35.900
Well?

00:19:36.550 --> 00:19:37.940
That is...

00:19:49.010 --> 00:19:50.500
It's not here either...

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:00.860
My knees hurt...

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:04.770
Snow...

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:14.800
I should go home.

00:20:36.690 --> 00:20:38.040
I'm home.

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:42.530
Chiaki, what are you doing...?

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:46.840
I've heard everything.

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:50.660
What...

00:20:55.090 --> 00:20:56.660
Why don't you open it?

00:20:58.380 --> 00:20:59.720
Opening...

00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:06.070
Kana-chan! Look! Look! It's a horsie!

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:06.900
Usa.

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:10.050
I won. I won. I won again!

00:21:10.050 --> 00:21:11.830
I've caught it, Minami.

00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:16.590
I heard you asked everyone to look for it?

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:21.590
I'm not really angry about the thing you broke.

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:24.600
You know that, right?

00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:29.860
I'm SO sorry!

00:23:30.630 --> 00:23:34.710
Have you ever found ice cream in the freezer but didn't know when it was put in?

00:23:34.710 --> 00:23:37.740
Frost forming on the surface makes you wonder if it can still be eaten.

00:23:37.740 --> 00:23:40.220
But, no worries. There's no expiration date for ice cream.

00:23:40.220 --> 00:23:42.490
Of course, I think it's more delicious if you eat it sooner.

00:23:42.490 --> 00:23:44.760
Ah, and if the ice cream starts to melt, you should finish it up right away.
